From 056a2aad62fc0300a608c5c96f036a5859cc63c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 16:48:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 003/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-common: raise max
 charge current to 3A

Matches downstream's own upper limit. The previous 1.5A was a
conservative placeholder pending thermal handling in the mainline
charging driver, which still doesn't exist - so this trades some
safety margin for charge speed; monitor battery/PMIC temperature
(info_carga.sh) during extended full-current charging.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
index ee13797fc..b77be88f0 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -38,11 +38,12 @@ battery: battery {
 		device-chemistry = "lithium-ion-polymer";
 
 		/*
-		 * Keep the maximum charging current conservative for now,
-		 * until we have thermal handling in the charging driver.
-		 * Downstream seems to have a upper limit of 3A.
+		 * Matches downstream's own upper limit of 3A. There's still
+		 * no thermal handling in the mainline charging driver, so
+		 * keep an eye on battery/PMIC temperature (info_carga.sh) if
+		 * you charge at the full 3A/15W for extended periods.
 		 */
-		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <1500000>;
+		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <3000000>;
 
 		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
 		voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4400000>;
